    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4df46a06_c31fe0ee",
        "filename": "drivers/base/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 538,
      "author": {
        "id": 1446383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-17T03:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like a locking issue, but I think it\u0027s fine because it is literally just a 32 bit read which is guaranteed to be atomic on all 32-bit or higher arch? Oh wait, this will be a 64-bit read though.\n\nEven in that case, I\u0027m wondering if I need to fix this. Because at worst case, the race happens as this device gets its last supplier linked to it and it\u0027s removed from the \"wait_for_suppliers\" list and it\u0027s put on the deferred probe list when it could have probed. But then it\u0027ll immediately be probed once the supplier device finishes probing.\n\nI\u0027m trying to avoid the locking here because rest of the code is in drivers/of/platform.c and we can\u0027t have drivers/base/core.c depend on it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 538,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 538,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "8b9d9c17a6793d2bc4502662038475e10701446e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56cd7f3a_96d7df28",
        "filename": "drivers/of/platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1446383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-17T16:46:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m going back and forth on whether this can cause a deadlock because I\u0027m holding the list lock while adding device links with AUTOPROBE_CONSUMER. I\u0027m wondering if I can end up in a nested of_platform_device_create_pdata(). Don\u0027t know if that\u0027s already not allowed (meaning I won\u0027t make it any worse) or if it can happen.\n\nThere are many ways to fix it. One being -- remove AUTOPROBE_CONSUMER) and fix the locking in device_links_check() when I check for !list_empty(). Another being doing the retry_link_to_suppliers() in a work queue.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
